<div class="article-body">
    <Fragment set:html={`<p>To dead hang, grip a pull-up bar overhand at shoulder width, step off with straight arms, set your shoulders and hold while breathing slowly. Stop one or two seconds before your grip gives out and step down under control.</p>

        <h2>Dead Hang Setup: What You Need</h2>
        <p>A pull-up bar is the only required equipment. The bar should sit high enough that your feet clear the ground with arms fully extended. A step or sturdy platform helps you reach the bar safely.</p>
        <p>Bar diameter affects grip comfort. Most pull-up bars are 28 to 32 mm (about 1.1 to 1.25 inches) across. Thicker bars are harder to hold.</p>
        <p>Chalk is optional. Gym chalk is magnesium carbonate. It dries the skin and increases friction between skin and bar. Use it if sweat, not fatigue, ends your hang. No study of chalk and dead hang time was found.</p>
        <p>Read the full <a href="/equipment-guide/">equipment guide</a> for pull-up bar options by mounting type.</p>

